# PesaTrack project-level npm configuration.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# npm 11.19 added a security feature that records which dependencies are allowed
# to run install scripts (the "allowScripts" field in package.json).
#
# This machine has a user-level setting in C:\Users\PC\.npmrc:
#     allow-scripts=@opencode/cli
# (created when the OpenCode CLI was installed). Expo's CLI forwards that
# resolved value to npm as an environment variable, and npm rejects it for
# project-scoped installs with the error:
#     EALLOWSCRIPTS --allow-scripts is not allowed in project-scoped installs
# which breaks `npx expo install`.
#
# A project-level .npmrc takes precedence over the user-level one, so setting
# the value to empty here keeps `npx expo install` working without changing any
# global configuration. An empty value means "no explicit policy", which is the
# same as a freshly created project on a clean machine.
#
# If a dependency later genuinely needs its install scripts approved, add it to
# the "allowScripts" field in package.json instead (see `npx approve-scripts`).
allow-scripts=
